    "title": "Free Sandbags Available for Local Homeowners at Los Angeles Fire Stations - NewsBreak",
    "text": "1 hours ago The Los Angeles Fire Department (LAFD) is offering free sandbags to homeowners in Los Angeles. Residents can collect up to 25 empty sandbags per household at any local fire station throughout the year. Sand is available at specific locations, including Fire Stations 5, 64, 91, 77, and the Sunland-Tujunga Municipal Building.\nLAFD states that sandbags work best to direct water and debris away from property, not to block water completely. The department recommends following safety guidelines when using sandbags. For large projects, residents should consider hiring licensed contractors. LAFD provides the sandbags and sand but does not fill, deliver, install, or remove them. Extra supplies are available at local home improvement stores.\nVisit here for more details This post includes content assisted by AI tools. Please refer to the source for verification and additional information. Learn more.\n1",
